(814701, 89853, 17233, '<td valign="top">I don''t know if it''s sheer brilliance or a deviate mind that can turn Tide to Shit so creatively. I love this - lots of humour and originality. Well done</td>', 'I don''t know if it''s sheer brilliance or a deviate mind that can turn Tide to Shit so creatively. I love this - lots of humour and originality. Well done', '2004-07-17 01:47:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(814716, 90598, 22011, '<td valign="top">This is a good character portrait, but I''m sorry to say, but it''s way outside the challenge...<br/> <br/>Looks like you''ve gota bit of motion blur in this shot, will be interested to see what iso/shutter/apeture you were using.  Obviously a reasonably small F number/large apeture as the background is nicely blurred, but I wonder if you couldn''t have changed your ISO setting up a couple of notches, or pushed it -1 stop?  The noice/grain of higher ISO would not have hurt this shot at all, and may have enhanced it a little, and pushing 1 or even 1.5 stops would have been OK as well as the shirt looks a little over exposed.<br/> <br/>Dunno what sort of camera you have, but on mine I can take a ''test'' metering without looking through the viewfinder, to see what shutter speed I''m metering, and it shows on the LCD on top of the camera, so I can change settings before annoying the ''model'' by pointing the obviously at them.<br/> <br/>Really nice photo, missed the challenge brief by a country mile, still giving it a 5 as I''m jealous of anyone who has the guts to do street photography like this.. :-).</td>', 'This is a good character portrait, but I''m sorry to say, but it''s way outside the challenge... Looks like you''ve gota bit of motion blur in this shot, will be interested to see what iso/shutter/apeture you were using.  Obviously a reasonably small F number/large apeture as the background is nicely blurred, but I wonder if you couldn''t have changed your ISO setting up a couple of notches, or pushed it -1 stop?  The noice/grain of higher ISO would not have hurt this shot at all, and may have enhanced it a little, and pushing 1 or even 1.5 stops would have been OK as well as the shirt looks a little over exposed. Dunno what sort of camera you have, but on mine I can take a ''test'' metering without looking through the viewfinder, to see what shutter speed I''m metering, and it shows on the LCD on top of the camera, so I can change settings before annoying the ''model'' by pointing the obviously at them. Really nice photo, missed the challenge brief by a country mile, still giving it a 5 as I''m jealous of anyone who has the guts to do street photography like this.. :-).', '2004-07-17 02:52:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(814718, 90200, 22011, '<td valign="top">This is a very interesting shot...  I''m not sure if I like it, but it''s certainly different.<br/> <br/>Your colour balance appears to be off though, and the two highlights on the right (your left) eye are a little hot and distracting.<br/> <br/>Her left (your right) cheek appears to be suffering from jpeg compression woes, or you pushed the contrast/brightness too far in your ediing program, and there are definate ''bands'' of colour from black to the skin tone.  Your image is only 65k, so you had quite a bit of room to move in terms of JPEG compresion, as the site limit is 150k.  If it''s a PS issue, and you greated the high-key look using curves, you probably need to re-shoot and try to get closer in the source image.  PS will do lots of things, but it''s not magic.<br/> <br/>You''ve got a great eye, and this shot shows that in it''s composition on the high-key tones.  Looking forward to seeing more....</td>', 'This is a very interesting shot...  I''m not sure if I like it, but it''s certainly different. Your colour balance appears to be off though, and the two highlights on the right (your left) eye are a little hot and distracting. Her left (your right) cheek appears to be suffering from jpeg compression woes, or you pushed the contrast/brightness too far in your ediing program, and there are definate ''bands'' of colour from black to the skin tone.  Your image is only 65k, so you had quite a bit of room to move in terms of JPEG compresion, as the site limit is 150k.  If it''s a PS issue, and you greated the high-key look using curves, you probably need to re-shoot and try to get closer in the source image.  PS will do lots of things, but it''s not magic. You''ve got a great eye, and this shot shows that in it''s composition on the high-key tones.  Looking forward to seeing more....', '2004-07-17 02:59:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(814726, 90460, 19608, '<td valign="top">Superb idea.  Everything works except the composition.  The frog sitting on the back of the other one just doesn''t work for me.  Exposure is perfect.  Neat font for the text too.</td>', 'Superb idea.  Everything works except the composition.  The frog sitting on the back of the other one just doesn''t work for me.  Exposure is perfect.  Neat font for the text too.', '2004-07-17 03:17:22.000000', NULL, 1),
